# The base images the CI test suites build from, each pinned by digest.
#
# Sourced by the suite scripts that build an image from an inline Dockerfile
# (dns-resolver, deb-install, rpm-install, tarball-install, mdns, native-api),
# which pass the pin in as a build argument. The Dockerfiles in the tree carry
# the same pins literally, since a Dockerfile cannot source a file; each says
# so beside its FROM. testing/check-base-pins.sh fails on a base that is not
# pinned, here or anywhere a CI image is built.
#
# Why pinned: a tag such as debian:12 moves with every rebuild of the image,
# so two runs of one tree could build on different bases, and a tree-identity
# skip (one green run standing for another of the same tree) would stand on a
# base the skipped run never saw. Each pin is the multi-arch index digest, so
# one value serves every architecture a leg runs on (the arm64 install leg
# included), and the readable tag stays in front of it. Docker resolves a
# digest through a pull-through mirror as it does a tag.
#
# To move one: read the current index digest with
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect <name:tag> --format '{{json .Manifest.Digest}}'
# or print them all with testing/check-base-pins.sh --current, replace the
# digest here and in the Dockerfiles that carry the same tag, and run the
# suites that use it. A pin delays a base image's security updates until it
# is moved, which is acceptable for test images; move them when a suite needs
# a newer base, and at least before each release.
#
# Digests read 2026-11-16.

DEBIAN12="debian:12@sha256:268fb24c39bca92d326dd83ea3abebe4a3f7751c804ffef23bb6d857dd343ff8"
